			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Centralize UriComponents construction with $mid marker\n\nAdd a shared UriComponents helper module ensuring every URI payload sent to the VS Code renderer carries the required `$mid: 1` marshalling marker. Without it, VS Code's IPC reviver leaves URIs as plain objects where `.fsPath` and `.with` are undefined, causing the sidebar and icon loader to silently fail.\n\nIntroduce FromFilePath, FromUrl, StampMidUri, and Normalize helpers that are now used consistently in handle_extensions_install (Extension.rs), handle_file_realpath (WindServiceHandler and WindServiceHandlers FileSystem.rs), and any other IPC handlers returning URI-shaped payloads. This prevents regression of the earlier extension location URI fix — inline json! builders elsewhere risked the same silent break in the renderer's URI revival chain.",
			"SHA": "954067a89bea76bac0cdeadc44dc0f80237a635a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T18:24:27Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "build(Project): Coordinate Element submodule updates across 4 components\n\nSynchronize Mountain, Output, Sky, and Wind submodules with the following changes:\n- Mountain: Fix extension location URI marshalling for VS Code renderer — VS Code's URI revival ignores objects without `$mid === 1` marker. Add Normalize_Location_To_UriComponents, Stamp_Mid_Uri, and Parse_File_Url_To_UriComponents functions. Extend BuildInitialUrl to recognize Mountain's `{uri:\"file://…\"}` format alongside VS Code's historical folderUri/workspace.configPath for backward compatibility.\n- Output: Document CopyNodeModules-StripDanglingSourceMap pairing rationale explaining why they're expressed as separate plugins with role-scoped matching.\n- Sky: Delegate build pipeline to Output plugins (Steps 1-7, 10-12, 14) via reusable plugin system. Move phase advancement from Astro script block into workbench.js to prevent chunk hoisting from delaying phases past Mountain's fallback timers. Remove ext-registry-probe as it's noisy. Gate missing browser bundle warnings behind LAND_WARN_MISSING_BROWSER_BUNDLES env var.\n- Wind: Complete polyfill re-export migration — Target/Polyfills/* files are now minimal re-export proxies delegating to @codeeditorland/output/Polyfill/* implementations.\n\nThis coordinated update delivers extension sidebar location resolution, build pipeline modularity, and polyfill consolidation while maintaining identical runtime behavior.",
			"SHA": "9cb4ed02baa8e78b5d031e934c3cc00804e0c569"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T17:26:22Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Project): Consolidate polyfill implementations into Output module\n\nSynchronize Element submodule to dccf43ce bringing a coordinated architectural refactor:\n- Output: Add Plugin module with CopyVSOutput, CopyVSRootFiles, SupplementFromDependency, CopyWorker, CopyNodeModules, StubUnpublishedAddons, CopyTauriMainProcessService copy plugins and StripCSSImport, InjectNameShim, ReplaceElectronIPCService, ReplaceSharedProcess, StaticToDynamicImport, ExtensionScannerIPC transform plugins\n- Sky: Update polyfill imports from @codeeditorland/wind/Target/Polyfills/* to @codeeditorland/output/Polyfill/*\n- Wind: Replace polyfill implementations with thin re-exports pointing to Output (ChildProcessPolyfill, FileProtocolShim, FileSystemPolyfill, IPCRendererShim, NativeModulePolyfill, ProcessPolyfill, SharedProcessProxy)\n\nThis eliminates duplicate code across the monorepo — polyfill fixes now only need to be made in Output to propagate to all consumers (Sky, Wind, Cocoon, and any future desktop shells).",
			"SHA": "9c28721e0d99588f2ee04793ce61415d61ab2e07"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
